how many videos should you do per week  so i got a question from a friend of  mine her name is bailey  and she's asking me how many videos  should she do per week to tell her story  now let me back up and tell you a little  bit about bailey  bailey has a successful company called  proactive movement  she's built this thing up over the past  couple years has had great results for  her clients they love her  she just feels like there's something  missing in her life like there's  something  more that she could give to the world  than what she's doing right now  her company will always be a part of her  she's always pouring energy into it but  but she's meant for something greater  and this is something that i think  everybody can relate to  at least i hope you can relate to right  do you feel like in your business or in  your life  you are meant for something greater than  what you're doing right now  and so i encourage you to say bailey you  need to document this  because what she's doing now is she's  going on a journey of self-discovery  she's trying a whole bunch of new stuff  she's traveling she's signing up for  courses  she's learning from mentors she's  practicing speaking she's practicing  videos she's trying out a whole bunch of  new stuff  to see where her path is this is really  important because for most people  they're afraid to take that step you  might be thinking to yourself  i i i don't know what i'm doing with my  life i feel like i deserve  better i feel like i could contribute  way more to this world  but you're too afraid to take the next  step  you're too afraid to start that journey  of exploration  so i told people you have to document  you got to record this  because i know you're gonna find your  path my friend bailey is gonna find her  path  she is gonna be a force to be reckoned  with in this world i know it  i believe it it's gonna happen but right  now  she doesn't know how it's all going to  work out she doesn't know what her path  is going to look like she doesn't know  who she's going to meet she doesn't know  what she's going to be doing  she's discovering and this is an  important journey  that everybody has to go on at least  once  in their life and this right now this is  the the  the most important part because  bailey in a couple years saying how she  became successful  is not his interest in the story what's  really important is this this is the  scary stuff  this is the uncertainty this is the  vulnerability this is the i don't know  what i'm doing now  that journey will help inspire  other people hopefully like you who are  going through the same thing but are too  afraid to take that step  seeing bailey do it will help inspire  others to take action with their own  life and so she writes to me and  says you know should i do it once a week  i don't know if that's  if that's too much to do i don't know if  i have enough to say in the week  so here's my two bits of advice and this  is for everybody who's trying to  document their journey  and get some stuff up on youtube or  wherever you're going to post it to help  inspire others  first of all you need to practice okay  one video per week should be  minimum minimum you want to be a speaker  you want to gain an audience you want to  build a movement  one video a week is a minimum  first of all because you need to  practice  you need to get better right as good as  bailey is  right now the people watching her videos  are just her friends sorry bailey i'm  being honest  but she has the potential  to impact millions of people and for  that to happen  she has to get better on camera now  she's done like two videos  and her her first two videos are way  better  than my first two videos she has a  natural ability  that is way better than what i started  with but she still has to get a lot  better and that comes from practice i've  gotten better with my videos because i  practice  i've done over a thousand videos you go  back even six months on my channel  and compare it with today and you'll see  the progress i wanna  i wanna remove my first videos because i  look back and  say oh my it's so bad that is so bad  but people still like them people still  watch them so i keep them up and it's  fun to see  how i've progressed through practice so  one per week is  minimum i do 14 per week  you got to do at least one per week okay  just to develop the skill set to get  better at speaking in front of the  camera and connecting with people  the second thing is this is really  important the types of videos that you  practice  so right now bailey's videos are  are summarizing what's happened to her  so i've taken this course and  and it was really great and now next  week i'm gonna go for this interview  and basically what she's doing with her  life and that that's great the problem  is  there's no feeling what would be way  more powerful  is take one moment that happened to you  in the past week  ideally you're recording it just after  it happened so it's still fresh  and just tell me about that moment  because your goal here is to make me  feel something good or bad  right most of us think about the good  things right i just landed this new deal  or i just signed up a new client or i  just got into this new program  or i just got a new mentor all the good  stuff right that's great  but the more powerful stuff is is on the  negative side  tell me about how nervous you are or how  scared you are  be vulnerable make me feel something  tell me one  story in depth and make me  feel like i'm with you right if you're  nervous i want to be nervous if you're  crying i want to be crying  take me on that journey instead of  summarizing what happened to you  and hopefully this gives you a lot more  stories to be able to practice and be  able to tell  the reason why it's so important is  because the goal of these videos  is not just to document your own  progress which is great  but to help inspire other people to do  the same thing  to help inspire millions of people to  look at their life and say i could do  better  and to inspire them and to move them to  action you have to make them  feel something if they don't feel  anything if they don't feel connection  to you they're not going to listen to  your advice  make them feel how important it is for  you  and draw them in and bailey's great at  this bailey isn't a  she has she wears her heart on her  sleeve she's she's  emotional which is great it just is not  coming across yet on camera  so this is a skill to practice so once a  week minimum  and instead of summarizing give me  specifics take me deep make me feel the  pain  make me feel the happiness bring me  along i want to be  deep inside your story make that happen  and you can connect with people and  you're starting your movement  belief so i'm clearly i'm sick and my  voice is really funny  but um i haven't recorded for the past  couple of weeks and evan has been  knocking on my door and saying why are  you recording anything and i've been  saying because i've been so busy  and he said no excuses you still need to  pump out one video a week when you're  feeling inspired when you're feeling  down when you're feeling busy no matter  what so yes i failed i'm here sick and  still recording  for those of you watching you liked the  video please give it a thumbs up below  let me know what you think if you agree  disagree leave it in the comments below  if you have a question  put it below make a video response and  if you want click on my face subscribe  to the channel  thank you guys so much i'll see you soon
 

